\title{shinyalcatraz: Build Portable, Zero-Admin-Install Shiny Apps for Locked-Down Environments}
\description{
Given a Shiny application, builds one or more self-contained, copy-and-run deployment bundles that require no administrator rights and no internet access on the target machine. Supports multiple build targets from a single app source: a pure-browser WebAssembly bundle (via 'shinylive'/'webR', no R install needed at all), a portable-R bundle (bundled R runtime + package library, launched via a local 'httpuv' server), and a native shell wrapper (via 'Tauri') for a double-click desktop/mobile experience across Windows, macOS, Linux, Android and iOS.
